00:58:52.200 --> 00:58:55.460
Maybe, maybe, but I let the alienists worry about that.

00:58:55.560 --> 00:58:56.560
My job is to catch them.

00:58:57.720 --> 00:58:59.420
And do you always catch them, Lieutenant?

00:58:59.740 --> 00:58:59.940
Well,

00:59:00.510 --> 00:59:01.550
Pretty good average, I guess.

00:59:03.090 --> 00:59:03.490
Oh, thanks.

00:59:14.720 --> 00:59:15.820
Something's stuck on your shoe.

00:59:18.150 --> 00:59:18.970
So there is.

00:59:20.430 --> 00:59:21.630
I'd known that I'd have changed them.

00:59:22.740 --> 00:59:23.460
Must be some mud.

00:59:24.200 --> 00:59:24.960
It looks like time.

00:59:30.960 --> 00:59:32.140
Yes, it is.

00:59:33.150 --> 00:59:34.150
Guess I got her on the pavement.

00:59:34.540 --> 00:59:35.220
Or on a roof.

00:59:36.320 --> 00:59:37.440
Roofs are covered with tar.

00:59:38.200 --> 00:59:39.800
I used to play on them every day when I was a kid.

00:59:39.920 --> 00:59:40.700
Cops and robbers.

00:59:40.840 --> 00:59:42.140
And I always played the robber.

00:59:42.380 --> 00:59:44.000
Now I make a living playing a cop.

00:59:44.560 --> 00:59:47.350
Shows you, you can't ever tell how a kid will wind up.

00:59:51.830 --> 00:59:52.410
Well, I...

00:59:53.780 --> 00:59:54.620
So I'd better be going.

00:59:55.960 --> 00:59:57.960
Strange, you didn't see anybody come in here.

00:59:58.310 --> 00:59:59.970
Oh, we picked up the cab...

01:00:00.090 --> 01:00:04.640
driver who drove the fellow we're looking for away from the robbery he says he let him off down the

01:00:04.640 --> 01:00:10.640
street and saw him run in here mind if i bring him in to take a look around oh he couldn't be here

01:00:10.760 --> 01:00:15.060
well then there won't be any harm done will there it's just one of those routine things won't take

01:00:15.060 --> 01:00:17.040
a minute i'll bring him in just a moment lieutenant

01:00:30.380 --> 01:00:33.380
In case you didn't know it, the house is surrounded by police.

01:00:33.950 --> 01:00:36.130
I assume that much. That's why I want you to help me.

01:00:36.780 --> 01:00:37.260
Help you?

01:00:37.620 --> 01:00:40.420
Yes. Go to the door and order them away.

01:00:41.790 --> 01:00:46.350
You and I will wait here for a while, and then we'll leave together, in case they don't obey.

01:00:47.340 --> 01:00:50.800
That would work all right, except, uh, what if I refuse to order them away?

01:00:51.270 --> 01:00:54.370
You forget. You told me the fellow you're looking for is desperate.

01:00:54.850 --> 01:00:55.570
Very desperate.

01:00:55.830 --> 01:00:57.270
Philip, you can't. You must...

01:00:57.270 --> 01:00:57.670
Oh, Philip, stop!

01:00:58.040 --> 01:00:58.300
Quiet!

01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:01.320
I haven't much patience, Lieutenant.

01:01:02.640 --> 01:01:06.460
Well, I haven't any alternative, have I?

01:01:08.270 --> 01:01:11.900
Yet I could just sit here and think it over for a moment, couldn't I?

01:01:12.360 --> 01:01:13.360
Yes, you could.

01:01:14.460 --> 01:01:17.640
But after a while, the police would become concerned about you.

01:01:18.060 --> 01:01:18.640
Break in.

01:01:24.820 --> 01:01:25.780
We're going out of here together.

01:01:26.630 --> 01:01:27.510
Go ahead and walk ahead of me.

01:01:27.510 --> 01:01:28.310
You don't know what you're doing!

01:01:28.530 --> 01:01:29.670
You can't do this! You can't!

01:01:30.280 --> 01:01:32.710
I'll go with you alone, but not them, not dad.

01:01:32.990 --> 01:01:34.210
We're going out of here together.

01:01:44.990 --> 01:01:47.630
I had to do it, even though he was your son.

01:01:48.340 --> 01:01:49.500
He wasn't my son.

01:01:51.470 --> 01:01:53.730
My son died two months ago.

01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:35.820
Benino, Benino, Benino, he's coming around.

01:02:36.080 --> 01:02:38.840
It's the first sign of life he's shown since the automobile accident.

01:02:39.130 --> 01:02:40.950
Concussion of the brain is a serious matter, Louise.

01:02:41.520 --> 01:02:43.000
For a while, I thought he'd never pull through.

01:02:43.810 --> 01:02:45.900
Benino, Benino, Benino.

01:02:58.470 --> 01:02:59.970
Thank heaven, he's coming out of his coat.

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:28.000
moment less. Try to move. Where? What? You've been in a coma for four days. Ever since your accident. Darling, I'm so glad you're better. So glad. You'll never know how glad I am. Nightmare. Horrible nightmare. What is it, darling?

01:03:30.510 --> 01:03:31.130
Nothing at all.
